# Linkagram context

Android app that resolves shared URLs, shows the redirect chain, extracts
coordinates from map links, and title summaries from allowlisted rich-link
hosts. Public demo of AI-assisted development. No backend.

- Canonical instructions: `AGENTS.md`. Behaviour is specified in `docs/specs/`;
  decisions in `docs/decisions/`. A spec wins over this rule.
- Before changing behaviour, read the matching spec. If none exists, write it.
- Do not add: backend, accounts, analytics, ads, cloud sync, WebView,
  JavaScript execution, Maps SDK, route building, location permissions, DI
  framework, extra Gradle modules.
- Optional local analysis history (Spec 006 / ADR-006) is in scope: Room +
  DataStore on device, off by default. Do not invent other persistence.
- Single module `:app`; boundaries are `core/`, `data/`, `domain/`, `ui/`.
- Add an abstraction only when something in the code needs it today.
  `HistoryRepository` is that concrete need for Spec 006.
